# Staging smoke-test environment — TEMPLATE. Copy, fill in, never commit.
#
#   cp infra/staging/staging.env.example infra/staging/staging.env
#
# infra/staging/staging.env is gitignored. Put the real key there and nowhere
# else: never on the command line (it lands in shell history and the process
# list), never in staging.env.example, never in a commit.
#
# This file is the SINGLE source of staging configuration. Every staging
# entrypoint loads it and nothing else:
#
#   infra/staging/run-stack.sh      starts the API / worker / Python service
#   infra/staging/migrate-staging.js  applies migrations
#   infra/staging/prove-targets.js    proves the targets are live and correct
#   infra/staging/run-smoke.sh        does all of the above, then the smoke test
#
# There is deliberately no second way to start a staging process. The old
# arrangement — remember to pass the right overrides on the command line — is
# what let a "staging" run come up silently attached to the shared database.

# Arms the boot-time target guard in apps/api/src/config/env.schema.ts and
# apps/api-python/src/config.py. Must be exactly "staging" or those guards stay
# dormant and the smoke test refuses to run.
#
# NOT the same variable as NODE_ENV. NODE_ENV=staging would be a reasonable
# value for a hosted staging deployment against a hosted database; AIOS_ENV
# means specifically "the disposable containers in docker-compose.yml".
AIOS_ENV=staging

# Reflects what this stack actually is. Kept distinct from AIOS_ENV above.
NODE_ENV=staging

# ── Postgres ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Matches infra/staging/docker-compose.yml. Throwaway credentials for a local,
# empty, loopback-only, RAM-backed database.
#
# BOTH must be set, and both must point at staging.
#
# schema.prisma declares `url = env("DATABASE_URL")` AND
# `directUrl = env("DIRECT_URL")`. Prisma MIGRATIONS use directUrl, not url. So a
# command that sets only DATABASE_URL leaves migrations pointed at whatever
# DIRECT_URL says — and packages/db/.env sets it to the shared Supabase
# instance. That is not an override problem (process env does win); it is a
# second variable that is easy to forget, and forgetting it is silent.
#
# Both guards now refuse that outcome rather than documenting it:
# migrate-staging.js verifies the datasource Prisma ACTUALLY resolved, and the
# boot guard refuses to start any staging process carrying a shared DIRECT_URL.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://aios_staging:staging_local_only@localhost:5433/aios_staging
DIRECT_URL=postgresql://aios_staging:staging_local_only@localhost:5433/aios_staging

# ── Redis ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port 6380, from docker-compose.yml. REQUIRED for staging.
#
# REDIS_URL is optional everywhere else: queue.module.ts and cache.service.ts
# fall back to redis://localhost:6379 and degrade gracefully, which is right for
# development. In staging that default silently attaches the API and worker to
# the developer's DEV Redis behind a log warning nobody reads — so the boot guard
# makes it mandatory when AIOS_ENV=staging.
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6380

# ── Allowlists ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The hosts staging is permitted to touch, as comma-separated host:port entries.
# There is no default — unset means nothing is nominated, so nothing is
# permitted and every guard fails closed.
#
# Nominate ONLY disposable staging infrastructure. Never a shared or hosted
# instance: the smoke test's checks 8 and 9 create and delete rows, and
# migrate-staging.js applies schema changes.
STAGING_DB_ALLOWLIST=localhost:5433
STAGING_REDIS_ALLOWLIST=localhost:6380

# ── Service-to-service ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Node -> Python internal contract. Must be the SAME value on both sides, and
# a different value from the one production uses.
PYTHON_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8000
INTERNAL_SERVICE_TOKEN=staging-only-internal-token-not-a-real-secret

# Any 32+ character throwaway value.
JWT_SECRET=staging-only-not-a-real-secret-32-chars-min

# ── Provider ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — a staging-scoped provider key with a low spend cap.
# Never a production key. The script prints its length, never its value.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# REQUIRED for check 2 (OCR multimodal). A publicly reachable image of legible
# printed text — the provider fetches this itself, so localhost and private
# hosts will not work.
#
# MUST be synthetic or consented material. Never a real student's answer sheet:
# that sends personal data to a third party outside the normal evaluation flow,
# with no offsetting benefit.
SMOKE_OCR_IMAGE_URL=

# Optional model overrides. Defaults to gpt-4o for both.
# SMOKE_EVAL_MODEL=gpt-4o
# SMOKE_OCR_MODEL=gpt-4o
